Privacy Policy for 11:11 – Wish Journal
Last Updated: May 5, 2025
	1.	Introduction
Welcome to 11:11 – Wish Journal (“we,” “our,” or “us”). Your privacy is important. This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, disclose, and protect your information when you use our iOS app. By installing or using 11:11 – Wish Journal, you agree to these terms.
	2.	Information We Collect
2.1 Personal Data You Provide

	•	Account Information (optional): If you create an account, we collect your email address.
	•	Wish Entries: Titles, descriptions, dates, and any photos you attach.
	•	Subscription Status: Your in‑app purchase receipts and subscription level.

2.2 Automatically Collected Data
	•	Usage Analytics: Anonymized data about how you interact with the app.
	•	Crash Reports: Stack traces and device/OS information if the app crashes.

2.3 Device & Log Data
	•	Device Identifiers: A randomized identifier generated by the app.
	•	System Data: Device model, OS version, and locale.
	•	Log Data: Timestamps of launches and errors.

	3.	How We Use Your Information

	•	To provide and maintain the app: Store and display your wishes and media.
	•	To manage premium features: Verify and restore subscriptions.
	•	To improve the app: Analyze usage and crash reports.
	•	To communicate (optional): Send updates or announcements if you’ve provided an email (you can opt out).

	4.	How We Share Your Information

	•	Third‑Party Services:
• Analytics provider (e.g., Firebase Analytics, Mixpanel) for anonymized data.
• Crash reporting service (e.g., Crashlytics).
	•	Legal Requirements: Disclosure if required by law or to protect our rights.
	•	No Sale of Personal Data: We do not sell or rent your information.

	5.	In‑App Purchases & Payment Data
All payments are handled by Apple’s In‑App Purchase system. We do not collect or store payment information—Apple manages billing, and we only receive purchase confirmations.
	6.	Data Retention
We retain your wish entries, media, and analytics data as long as your account is active or as needed to provide services. If you delete the app and do not restore it, local data is removed; to delete server‑stored data, contact us.
	7.	Security
We use industry‑standard measures (HTTPS, secure storage) to protect your data. However, no method is 100% secure.
	8.	Your Rights & Choices

	•	Access & Correction: You can view or edit your entries in the app.
	•	Delete Account/Data: Email us to request permanent deletion of your account and data.
	•	Email Communications: Opt out of promotional emails via unsubscribe link or by contacting us.

	9.	Children’s Privacy
This app is for users aged 13 and older. We do not knowingly collect data from children under 13. If you believe we have collected such data, contact us for deletion.
	10.	Changes to This Policy
We may update this policy to reflect changes in practices or law. We will post the updated date at the top when changes occur.
